---
import Base from '$lib/layouts/Base.astro';
import groq from './groq.svg';
import skyclient from './skyclient.svg';
import vanta from './vanta.svg';
import originality from './originality.svg';
import surplus from './surplus.svg';
import svgo from './svgo.svg';
---

<Base title="Notable affiliations">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      <em
        >This page is a list of my most notable affiliations. It admittedly looks like a resume, but
        I genuinely had fun at each of these places.</em
      >
    </p>
    <h2><img {...surplus} title="Surplus Intelligence" /> September 2026 - now</h2>
    <p>Surplus Intelligence is a marketplace for discounted inference capacity.</p>
    <p>
      Provided 80B+ tokens of capacity. Created pipeline to automatically research and organize
      support tickets. Created automation using highly efficient models to automatically ban
      scammers.
    </p>
    <h2><img {...originality} title="Originality" /> January 2025</h2>
    <p>Originality is one of the most accurate AI detectors on the market.</p>
    <p>
      Produced report on how well Originality detects base LLM output, measuring the effects of
      different topics, prompts, and detectors.
    </p>
    <h2><img {...groq} title="Groq" /> May 2024 - December 2025</h2>
    <p>
      Groq was an AI inference service built on fast custom LPU hardware. Its talent was acquired
      and designs were licensed in 2025 by NVIDIA.
    </p>
    <p>
      Participated in GroqChamp community devrel program. Assisted Discord users with technical
      support, both manually and with a custom context menu bot, until Groq was consumed by NVIDIA.
    </p>
    <h2>
      <img {...svgo} title="SVGO" /> November 2023 - now
    </h2>
    <p>SVGO is an open source optimizer for SVGs. It arguably is the best one out there.</p>
    <p>
      Contributed novel optimizations like reducing redundancy around <code>z</code>, converting
      arcs to lines, converting cubic beziers to quadratic beziers, and numerous other bug fixes and
      assurances.
    </p>
    <h2>
      <img {...vanta} title="Vanta" /> February 2023 - ~November 2023
    </h2>
    <p>Vanta was a community of Minecraft malware (mostly infostealer) researchers.</p>
    <p>
      Worked together to understand novel and obscure malware and obfuscation methods. Built
      personal static analyzer <a href="https://github.com/KTibow/RatRater2">RatRater 2</a> and personally
      terminated exfiltration webhooks.
    </p>
    <h2>
      <img {...skyclient} title="SkyClient" /> March 2022 - April 2023, ~August 2023 - April 2024
    </h2>
    <p>
      SkyClient was an alternative to traditional Hypixel clients that let you build your own
      modpack. It was replaced by Polyfrost's OneClient when Hypixel removed support for Minecraft
      1.8.9 in February 2026.
    </p>
    <p>
      Maintained server, support tickets, and data repository. Created bot that performed various
      maintainence functions, including providing automatic solutions to tickets using NLP
      technology. Created info website (skyclient.co) and an installer in the novel form factor of a
      web app (Mart). Contributed Bayes-based anti-spam logic to first party mods.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    align-self: center;
    margin: 1rem;
  }
  h2 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;

    > img {
      width: auto;
      height: 1em;
    }
  }
</style>
